Z||000000||recluse||10-22-2001||11:57 PM||||OK well maybe not almost... but he didn't win by much. It could have been a dodge stealth, I know some of them looked close to a 3000GT...  I pull up next to him at the light and look over and see "twin turbo" on the side, and think to myself "Hes gonna dust me" But I decide to go for it anyways.  As the light was ready to change he started revving up and I could hear the turbo spooling up.  I jumped off the line first and by the time I was changing to 2nd he was right beside me and "slowly" pulling past me, then when he switched to 2nd (rather slowly, and with all kinds of turbo lag) I was back side by side with him, and then he just pulled away. <P>The whole time there was this chick sticking her head out of the passenger side franticly slapping the roof of the car. <P>Are those cars really that slow with twin turbo, or did the dude just not know how to drive?  He shoulda spent his money on a Fiero and added a turbo.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||BlackStang95||10-23-2001||12:28 AM||||ROTFLMAO about the girl slapping the car, I'd guess he has a mechanical problem or couldnt drive.  They are very fast.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||10-23-2001||12:54 AM||||there heavy cars (Dannyboy?)<P>I had an altercation with a stock one that is owned by the local stereo shop. He had a hard time pulling on me below 40mph.<P>Same as my Friends old 400hp 300zx TT. Even til about 40mph. Then his bost comes on , his wheels spin and he's gone. In town on short drag races I can sit right beside him until the upper end of 2nd gear (4spd box in my car)<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000003||SLYGUY||10-23-2001||04:31 AM||||I had a '85 3000GT briefly. <BR>Mine wasn't the Twin Turbo model, but it had everything else. <BR>From what I can remember, it was a 200hp three liter six cylinder.<BR>Bummer was that the motor was hooked up to a transaxle that drove the front wheels. I think it is a little silly to make a sports car front wheel drive. Almost as silly was the rear seats. Pretty much upholstered dimples. You would never put anyone back there that you actually care about.<BR>Car was very smooth and had 160+mph top end. <BR>Not much acceleration with the automatic.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000004||falconhulk||10-23-2001||08:26 AM||||ok, the stealth did not just look like the 3000gt ...it was the 3000 gt.  a joint project by Dodge and Mistu.  The twin turbo model was extremely fast!  Check the specs on it by doing a search for 0 to 60 times.  I dont understand your post.  If you heard that turbo spool already before he launced there would not have been any lag by the time he shifted to 2nd.  How old was this guy?  Only thing I can figure is he was a kid that did not know how to drive or his clutch was slipping bid time.  Did he do a big burnout?  You let those cars spool up and drop the hammer.....they spin the tires hard.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Galen||10-23-2001||10:04 AM||||My brother had a 93 Stealth, the back seats were 'fun' to get into and out of.. specially on a 2k mile round trip  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> 'm 6'3 and had very little problems, however. 222hp out of the es model.. 140mph seems really fast looking from the back seat, at night, in the streets of Atlanta..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B>Ray</B> Webmaster of <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A><BR>"The price of love is tragedy"||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula||10-23-2001||10:29 AM||||I've only rode in a modified one. (danny Boy's) and it is FAST.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||recluse||10-23-2001||05:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I dont understand your post.  If you heard that turbo spool already before he launced there would not have been any lag by the time he shifted to 2nd.  How old was this guy?  Only thing I can figure is he was a kid that did not know how to drive or his clutch was slipping bid time.  Did he do a big burnout?  You let those cars spool up and drop the hammer.....they spin the tires hard.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I heard the turbo before he took off but he didn't spin at all... Just a kid that didn't know what he was doing. When he changed to 2nd it took another second for the turbo to kick back in, and then he pulled away pretty fast.<P><p>[This message has been edited by recluse (edited 10-23-2001).]||||reg||1
