Z||000014||danny boy||10-23-2001||10:31 PM|||| Oh,gee, who'd a guessed I'd post on here? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>  <BR>  In stock form mine ran a best of 14.26. 100K miles on it. They weigh a ton(two)and with age, shifting is a big problem.  <BR>  Like Ed Parks told me: "you could have done a lot to the Fiero with that money."<P>   SLYGUY, thats a 222 hp 3.0L V6.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR> <BR>THEY ARE NOT SPORTS CARS!! THEY ARE GT CARS!!! (sorry, pet peeve)<BR>   Ya can't really burn tires... its AWD. Well, you can, but the expensive trans noises aren't worth it.<P> batt- trust me- stick with your Fiero.<P> In case anyone cares, My best time to date was a 13.37 @ 104(?) and a 13.47 @ 107. On the first run I got a 2.1 60' time, and the second I got a 2.2. A friend up there who has less than half the mods I do was pulling 1.8 & 1.9 60' and 13.4 was his best. But then again, he knows how to launch.<BR>   I ran out of track time this year so I didn't get to run with the stock injectors and the exaust problem fixed. I was running so rich it looked like a dump truck taking off. When I had the exaust done the Guy shoved the pipe so far into the cat that it mashed the webbing!!! And I thought it was just the Flowmaster...<BR>   ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Galen||10-24-2001||01:35 AM||||Jaei Sun, I dont like you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I can attest to the cost of the trannys, I saw the receipt for my brothers after it let go.. glad I got an old pontiac hehe<P>------------------<BR><B>Ray</B> Webmaster of <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A><BR>"The price of love is tragedy"||||reg||1
Z||000016||Ambush||10-25-2001||01:55 AM||||I used to own a Stealth Twin turbo and there is NO WAY a fiero could keep up in any gear. Don't get me wrong...my fiero is fun to drive, but it is nowhere as fast as the Stealth.||||reg||1
Z||000017||AutoXdbdragSE||10-25-2001||03:18 PM||||Slammed Fiero...  How?<BR>300zx twin turbo.. 0-60 5.6 seconds<BR>Fastest stock fiero.. 0-60 7.6 seconds<P>and if i remember right the fiero 4 speed with v-6 in 85 would reach 60 at the top of 2nd gear.. so assuming by near top you ment 1-2k short of redline your sayint it takes at least another 2 seconds to finish... i'm thinkin the 300 would walk you a while before 60.<P>Oh and i think 300's reach close to 50 in first..||||reg||1
Z||000018||Slammed Fiero||10-25-2001||03:50 PM||||No idea.. I could launch a lot harder than he could. He owns an import aftermarket place , infact Fiero lisa Bought her wheels from him.<P>Raced him over and over one night just for fun. He car was a dead mule under 40mph. He had a greddy system on the car with no cat converters, the boost was cranked and it ran a best of 13.7.<P>He has since sold the car and moved onto a low mile 92 240 SX. The car has 300ZX front brakes on it , full suspension , but the motor is bone stock. A lot lighter better balanced car.<P>I pulled several mid 6 sec passes (a few with the owner of the 300zx in the car) with a GTEC. We got mid 5's out of his car , too much wheel spin though.<P>here is his new car along with a 12.3 Sec 1/4 mile eagle talon. For those who think the AWD is a huge advantage , it pulls 1.8 60 ft times. Not really that earth shattering. I have seen stock Fiero's pull sub 2 60 ft times<P>The talon has 375Hp at the wheels<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mach1motorsports.ca/pics." TARGET=_blank>www.mach1motorsports.ca/pics.</A> <P>and no I wouldn't attempt to race the talon. Fun car to ride in though!<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000019||danny boy||10-25-2001||04:48 PM|||| I can attest to the sub 40 MPH thing. I may as well get out and push til the turbos spool.<BR> I also agree with the launch thing. While AWD does eliiminate a great deal of wheelspin(letting us launch at a higher RPM, thus turbos spool faster) it also weighs a lot more and has more parasitic drag. My personal best 60' time is only a 2.01,and I have seen 3/S cars with 1.7 at best.<BR>Consideriny my POS weighs 3960# with 1/2 tank and me in it, Its no wonder it has nothing off the line, even with max TQ @ a little under 3000RPM.Bet I could pull stumps outta the ground,though. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
